{"tool_name":"fatslim","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"FATSLiM","home":"http://fatslim.github.io/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software to analyze Molecular Dynamics simulations of membranes.","addition_date":"2019-08-04T09:43:28Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:24Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:FATSLiM","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"sebastien.buchoux@u-picardie.fr","name":"S\u00e9bastien Buchoux","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://pythonhosted.org/fatslim/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Document clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3279"},{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"FATSLiM","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw563","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2016. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.When studying biological membranes, Molecular Dynamics (MD) simulations reveal to be quite complementary to experimental techniques. Because the simulated systems keep increasing both in size and complexity, the analysis of MD trajectories need to be computationally efficient while being robust enough to perform analysis on membranes that may be curved or deformed due to their size and/or protein-lipid interactions. This work presents a new software named FATSLiM ('Fast Analysis Toolbox for Simulations of Lipid Membranes') that can extract physical properties from MD simulations of membranes (with or without interacting proteins). Because it relies on the calculation of local normals, FATSLiM does not depend of the bilayer morphology and thus can handle with the same accuracy vesicles for instance. Thanks to an efficiency-driven development, it is also fast and consumes a rather low amount of memory.","authors":[{"name":"Buchoux S."}],"citationCount":59,"date":"2017-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"FATSLiM: A fast and robust software to analyze MD simulations of membranes"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Lipids","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0153"},{"term":"Literature and language","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3068"},{"term":"Membrane and lipoproteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0820"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"FATSLiM","home":"https://bio.tools/FATSLiM","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software to analyze Molecular Dynamics simulations of membranes.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:fatslim/cmd/fatslim.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":70,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":2,"year":"2018"},{"count":4,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2026"},{"count":6,"year":"2024"},{"count":7,"year":"2020"},{"count":9,"year":"2025"},{"count":10,"year":"2021"},{"count":10,"year":"2022"},{"count":16,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw563","pmid":"27578804","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"FATSLiM: a fast and robust software to analyze MD simulations of membranes.","year":2016}]}],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":